  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A dumbbell in a gym has a mass of $1\\,\\text{kg}.$ What is this mass in grams?",
  "worked_solution": "A table showing the units of mass in metric units is given below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilogram | $\\text{kg}$ | $1\\,\\text{kg}=1\\,000\\,\\text{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\text{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\text{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}=1\\,\\text{g}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{kg}$ is equivalent to $1\\,000\\,\\text{g}.$",
